  "spiritual_reading": "\n\n\n#\n Spiritual\n Translation\n of the Chapter\n\n\n---\n\n\n**\n¶1.\n** …\nthe in\nmost nature within\n …\n is the state\n of the\n mind\n in\n which …\n and\n … their ou\ntermost boundary\n.\n\n**¶2.**\n What\n the inmost nature of this\n reality\n is\n —\n no finite\n understanding could\n re\ncount or dis\nclose,\n nor\n say\n in\n what manner\n it has\n existed\n from\n eternity — all things\n …\n and … dis\nclose … eternity …\n great\nness … and\n again\n the … tend toward\n …\n the origin\n of what\n is eternal\n and the boundary\n of what is eternal\n …\n that\n one is\n set\n down.\n\n**¶3.\n** The state of spiritual\n death …\n the quality\n of the in\nmost nature … which exists from\n ev\nerlasting to\n everlasting …\n within\n … with one another.\n\n**\n¶4.** As for the perpet\nuity of evil\n and\n falsity which exists from the\n most\n ancient origin\n, no finite\n understanding is\n able to compreh\nend how they\n subs\nist. For no other power was ever\n disclosed\n to them by\n which\n anything\n could speak or recount their\n origin or\n manner\n of existence. However, from the time\n when evil\n stirred itself and rose up\n against wisdom\n,\n seeking\n to come and dom\ninate the state\n of those\n who possess\n spiritual\n life —\n\n\n**¶5.** —\n the\n Divine\n Truth going\n forth to\n combat came\n out\n against it and held\n it back;\n he kept it separate from the interior\n mind\n where\n spiritual\n life dwells. He held it back\n. From that time, when wisdom was\n inter\nmingled with falsity, and spiritual\n life with spiritual death, it became possible\n to speak and to\n dis\nclose how the assault\n and the spiritual\n conflict came\n to\n pass —\n how wisdom was entwined with fals\nity —\n which is\n the ent\nanglement of life\n within\n death.\n\n**¶6.\n** After\n evil\n stirred itself in its own in\nmost nature, its\n intention\n …\n within\n its own state\n.\n It … the entire realm\n of falsity in its …\n of wisdom\n in the abyss of\n the lowest\n hell\n. For the inmost nature within\n it …\n because …\n they reckoned … on its side\n … this first quality\n of\n evil\n …\n because the\n external\n form of its nature\n was\n hard\nened beyond\n any\n resistance\n that\n exists\n in the created\n universe.\n\n**¶7.\n** …\nof\n spiritual\n death … envy,\n which is\n the hatred\n of all\n good …\n the\n realm of falsity … deliber\nation\n within\n …\n wickedness … for\n as it … the injuries\n to\n spiritual\n life … against this realm of\n good\n and\n truth …\n\n\n**¶8.** Then\n he will rush\n …\n from the realm of …\n falsity. It drew away\n …\n his particular\n faculties … is deep … within\n them.\n\n**¶9.\n** It\n spread itself throughout\n all\n things\n. It generated from\n itself\n five\n fundamental principles of evil: dense falsity\n arising\n from evil\n,\n self-love,\n reasoning from falsity, truth\n fals\nified and\n inv\nerted, and utter negation of\n all\n good\n. From\n these\n it\n sprouted dist\norted perceptions.\n It came up and\n formed itself within\n its\n own state\n;\n it generated from\n itself by\n successive\n deriv\nation\n in\n inn\numerable emanations, none\n resemb\nling another\n.\n In\n the deep\nest repositories\n of hell\n, it brought\n forth many evil\n affections —\n destruct\nive\n impul\nses,\n falsities born\n of the\n l\nust for\n domin\nion, and savage\n appet\nites of\n every\n kind. It\n was established and grew powerful\n in the hid\neous forms that\n belong\n to fals\nity:\n dark\n,\n and\n by their\n fury\n, by\n their wickedness and mutual\n hatred, they destroy one\n another even\n as they war among\n themselves.\n\n**¶10.\n** Then the deliber\nation of the ruling evil humbled its\n own\n realm and all\n its powers. It perceived\n the nature of divine\n wisdom.\n It conspired to wage spiritual\n combat\n against the exalted kingdom of\n heaven\n and\n its\n glory\n.\n\n**¶11.**\n However\n, He\n —\n the Divine\n Love\n itself\n,\n the Father of all\n that\n is great\n — knew also\n of this\n war, of\n the intention\n to disturb the realm of wisdom.\n In the\n depth\n of His\n own\n divine\n wisdom He\n transformed Himself and\n went\n forth against it.\n\n**¶\n12.** Indeed\n, at that time … to\n go\n forth\n against …\n the\n Divine\n …\n\n\n**¶13.** From\n within\n itself\n it poured forth\n its\n nature\n into\n the fundamental\n principles\n of evil\n: into\n dense falsity, into self-love\n, into reasoning from falsity, into\n falsified truth, and\n into utter negation. It rose\n up from the deep\nest hell, establishing\n itself within\n dist\norted perceptions that\n stood\n arr\nayed against wisdom\n.\n\n\n**¶14.** Also\n, at the time when evil\n generated\n itself further\n, it formed works\n of\n its\n own kind\n,\n being established\n within\n them. Then\n the\n five external truths were\n summoned —\n the tru\nths derived\n from the Divine Truth who\n goes forth to combat — the sons of\n the First Man.\n\n**¶\n15.** And at the time when\n evil generated itself from those\n works through its offspring, they fell into\n the natural mind and drew strength from the\n fundamental principles of\n evil and were nourished by them\n —\n wickedness together\n with cruelty —\n all\n concentrated\n within the ruling evil,\n the chief\n of all particular\n evils. He subjected\n his realms and his\n powers;\n he gathered them all into himself. He\n made\n himself ready for spiritual\n combat;\n he set himself to war\n against\n the\n state\n of mind\n illumin\ned\n by wisdom, and against\n the great\n sovereign\n Divine\n Love who dwells within\n it.\n\n**¶16.\n** At that very moment the Divine Truth\n going\n forth to combat drew\n near to his external truths —\n the divine principles that shine with\n their\n own light. He spoke with them,\n that\n he might entrust to\n them a charge\n;\n he disclosed\n to them and\n taught them everything\n concerning\n what\n was\n to come\n. He assumed them upon\n himself. He arranged them in\n order. He cloth\ned himself\n with them,\n one\n truth\n over\n another,\n upon\n his own\n fac\nulties and\n powers\n — facing\n the danger\n —\n from\n the highest\n states\n of the mind —\n against\n evil\n with\n all its powers — from\n the beginning\n,\n it\n being beyond\n all measure\n.\n\n---\n\n*\nA\n note on method\n:* The\n \"\nfive\n dark\n elements\" (\nsmoke, fire, wind, water,\n darkness) consistently\n correspond\n to the five fundamental falsities and ev\nils by\n which the\n h\nells operate\n:\n dense falsity obsc\nuring understanding\n, self-love consuming\n the will, sophist\nical\n reasoning per\nverting thought\n, truth\n inv\nerted and falsified to\n serve\n evil, and the\n \nutter absence\n and\n negation of all good and\n truth. Their\n opposition\n by\n \"\nfive\n garments\" corresponds\n to the five external truths with\n which the Divine clothes\n itself to\n enter\n combat —\n each\n one\n answ\nering its\n opposite\n.\n The entire\n chapter\n describes\n,\n in spiritual\n reality\n, the process\n by which evil first\n st\nirs from\n its own nature, attempts\n to dom\ninate the regener\nating\n mind, and is\n met\n by the Divine Truth proce\neding from Divine\n Love,\n who\n clothes\n himself\n in\n accommod\nated\n truths in\n order to engage\n in the\n spiritual combat that\n makes\n redem\nption possible.",
